 "model": "lora",
 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty years,\nThe love I had for thee; it has forgotten\nTo be contented again.\nLike the sun set on a darkening day,\nLike a light cloud in death or pleasure gone,\nOne thought of thy face to me; that alone\nIs life.  How shall I live then? alone?\nWhat, no one ever come and kiss again,\nNo more understand I by translation\nHow oft thou hast gazed at myself\nFor beauty's rapture, with desire\nOf other eyes than mine to behold",
